DOCX equations keep every double-struck letter and digit

Word marks a math run double-struck with m:scr and shows its letters
and digits as Unicode's double-struck characters. The OMML import kept
only C, N, Q, R and Z, as Starmath's set symbols, and wrote every
other character plain, so a double-struck 3 came back as 3 (Ely
R15.11g). The other letters and digits now become their double-struck
Unicode characters, which Word shows unchanged; lowercase c, n, q, r
and z no longer become the unknown names setc and the like.
A run marked as normal text (m:nor) stays plain, as Word shows it.
Quotes inside a normal-text run are escaped, so they stay. A literal
run (m:lit) keeps its math letters; only m:nor makes Starmath text.
